# Smart To-Do List

An interactive, responsive To-Do List built with **HTML, CSS and JavaScript** (no libraries) as a mini project in my internship learning phase.

## Features
- Add tasks with **priority** (Low / Medium / High) and **due date**
- **Edit** a task (pencil button or double-click), press Enter to save, Esc to cancel
- Mark tasks as done, delete tasks, **clear completed**, delete all
- **Search**, **filter** (All / Active / Done) and **sort** (Newest / Due date / Priority)
- **Overdue** tasks are highlighted in red
- **Progress bar** with percentage of completed tasks
- **Dark mode** (remembers your choice)
- Data is saved in the browser (localStorage), so it stays after refresh
- Input validation, duplicate check, accessible labels, responsive layout

## Concepts Practiced
- Semantic HTML and accessibility (labels, aria attributes)
- CSS variables, Flexbox, media queries, animations, theming
- DOM manipulation and event handling
- Arrays and objects: `map`, `filter`, `sort`, `some`, `forEach`
- Date handling, `localStorage` with JSON and error handling
- Security: `textContent` instead of `innerHTML` for user input

## How to Run
1. Download or clone this repository
2. Open `index.html` in any browser

